{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Magic Lens.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Magic Lens.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"magic lens magic lens","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Magic Lens.md","fileName":"Magic Lens.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Magic Lens","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Tangible and Multimodal Interaction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Tangible and Multimodal Interaction","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Magic Lens.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Magic Lens.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"magic lens magic lens","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Magic Lens.md","fileName":"Magic Lens.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Magic Lens","heading":"Magic Lens","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A magic lens is a movable interface region that changes how information inside its boundary is displayed. In AR, a tracked handheld or virtual lens can reveal hidden structure, apply a filter, or present additional detail while the surrounding view remains unchanged.\n\nThe lens position and orientation become spatial input. Its boundary makes the transformation local and understandable, although holding, aiming, and coordinating the lens with another task can impose physical effort.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Tangible and Multimodal Interaction","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Magic Lens.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Magic Lens.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"magic lens magic lens","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Magic Lens.md","fileName":"Magic Lens.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Magic Lens","heading":"References","sectionNumbe